BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Promise: Untold Stories of SC's Black Patriots
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261115T171500
UID:10003223-1794754800-1794762900@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/10/The-Promise-BRAC-Flyer-Final.png
CATEGORIES:Events,Performance
DESCRIPTION:Set during the Revolutionary War\, Six Black Patriots from Sou
 th Carolina are captured by British forces during the Siege of Charleston\
 ; a pivotal battle that serves as a victory for the British and Loyalist f
 orces. As the pressure of captivity intensifies\, the soldiers are left be
 hind only to realize a broader struggle that will determine their fate. Wi
 ll their promise of freedom\, liberty\, and life be in the hands of the Co
 ntinental Army\, or will the British Crown rule?
LOCATION:Broad River Arts Center\, 1500 Broad River Road\, Columbia\, SC\,
  29210\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/the-promise-untold-stories-of-scs-b
 lack-patriots/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Screening of "Our Story\, Too: Women\, Native Americans and Africa
 n Americans in the Revolutionary War."
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T130000
UID:10003233-1794916800-1794920400@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2026/11/The-Untold-Heroes-of-the-Revolution-Our-Story-Too_CALENDAR.jpg
CATEGORIES:Film,Movie,Movie Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Anderson County Museum on November 17 at noon o
 r at 5:30 PM to enjoy a screening of “Our Story\, Too: Women\, Native Am
 ericans and African Americans in the Revolutionary War.” This documentar
 y uncovers the often-untold contributions of women\, Native Americans\, an
 d African Americans during the Revolutionary War\, highlighting individual
 s with South Carolina ties through expert commentary and dramatic reenactm
 ents. \nIt was produced by SCETV with production funding provided by the S
 outh Carolina American Revolution Sestercentennial Commission (SC250).
LOCATION:Anderson County Museum\, 202 East Greenville Street\, Anderson\, 
 SC\, 29621\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/screening-of-our-story-too-women-na
 tive-americans-and-african-americans-in-the-revolutionary-war/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lunch & Learn: The Charleston Patriots: Strangers in a Strange Lan
 d
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261117T133000
UID:10003172-1794916800-1794922200@southcarolina250.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://southcarolina250.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2026/08/Ryals-11.17-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lunch and Learns
DESCRIPTION:A few months after the surrender of Charles Town in 1780 the B
 ritish rounded up and arrested sixty-three of the most prominent leaders o
 f the Revolutionary movement in South Carolina despite pledging on their h
 onor that they would not violate the terms of their parole. They were sent
  to East Florida where they were held against their will under town arrest
  in St. Augustine as prisoners of war for 9 months. \nRobert Ryals returns
  to the Rev War Visitor Center to share this dramatic and sometimes amusin
 g historic storytelling experience based on the diary and experiences of J
 osiah Smith\, a Charles Town merchant. \nRSVP @ simplyrevolutionary.com \n
 You bring your lunch and we will provide the learning opportunity!
LOCATION:Revolutionary War Visitor Center\, 212 Broad Street\, Camden\, SC
 \, 29020\, United States
URL:https://southcarolina250.com/event/lunch-learn-the-charleston-patriots
 -strangers-in-a-strange-land/
END:VEVENT
